# stale-eye.xrs - the deterministic one-sided tag stream, and the runtime's answer to it.
#
# Under `stereo reentry` a projection submit names each eye's swapchain, and the
# compositor shows that swapchain's most recently RELEASED image. When pass 1
# tags its present (-1) and pass 2 is skipped, the LEFT is rewritten every
# other present while the RIGHT keeps showing a held image: the 2026-09-03
# headset desync ("the judder stays in the left eye and stops in the right").
# `camera postest` trips the pass-2 test gate on every tick, so it reproduces
# the one-sided stream on demand without a pause menu.
#
# The sim classifies every projection submit: projStaleSubmits counts a
# two-swapchain submit whose eye was released in an earlier frame. Before the
# 41.1 gate fix this sequence FAILS at the first stale assert with `vrpace
# strict off` (the instrument can print the unwelcome answer), passes with
# strict on (the fallback shows the fresh eye to both eyes: projMonoSubmits
# climbs instead), and passes with strict off once the gates are decided once
# per tick. Needs GAMEPLAY (the sewers) - the pass-2 gates refuse a menu.
reset
@mod stereo reentry
@frames 300
@assert sessionState eq FOCUSED
@assert projectionViews eq 2
@assert eyeSameSwapchain eq False
@assert eyeAgeL le 0
@assert eyeAgeR le 0
@assert projStaleSubmits eq 0
@mod camera postest 30 0 0
@frames 200
@assert projStaleSubmits eq 0
@mod camera postest stop
@frames 200
@assert eyeAgeL le 0
@assert eyeAgeR le 0
@assert projStaleSubmits eq 0
@mod stereo mono
